body:
The grouped invoices have run for about two weeks, and the agent looked at whether it is time to clean up. The setting USAGE_GROUPING is read in five places: the line builder, the preview job, the admin tool's invoice page, the CSV export and one test helper.

Before removing anything, the agent checked the facts of the two weeks. There were 14 evening runs, with about 3,100 invoices in total. No customer ticket mentioned the lines, and finance had not raised a question after the first week.

There is one open item: Ines has not yet checked a full month with the grouped invoices, since the month is not over. She will do it at the month's end, and the agent wants to keep the setting until then, since a switch back is the quick way out if she finds something.

The checklist for the removal is:
- delete the old branch in the line builder and keep the grouping as the only path;
- remove the setting from the preview job, the admin tool and the export;
- make the test helper call the grouping directly;
- delete the comparison test that runs both modes, but keep the quantity sum test;
- remove the setting from the config files and the deployment notes.

The CSV export deserves a thought. It reads the raw usage rows, and so it never depended on the grouping, but it checks the setting to print a note. The note can go.

The agent also thought about whether any customers have asked for the full detail of usage. The portal has a usage page with the daily counts per product, so the detail is available there, and the invoice only needs the summary.

The agent wrote the plan into the notes folder with the condition: remove after Ines has accepted the month. The work itself is about two hours.
